      "q": "7. Sheila asked the children \u201cAre you ready to do the work?\u201d",
      "a": "Sheila asked the children if they were ready to do the work.\nClass 9 English Beehive Chapter 5 The Snake and The Mirror - A Summary\nFollowing the narrative technique of a story within a story, Beehive Chapter the Snake and the Mirror is a humorous tale that shows how a homeopath doctor assesses himself humorously and critically. The main idea of the story revolves around two aspects, which are the snake and the mirror.\nThe story adds a funny twist when the terrified doctor realises that the snake was least interested in attacking him but rather fascinated by its own reflection. Thus, it resulted in the doctor\u2019s life being saved. The central message of the story highlights the fact that pride or vanity are virtues that cause one harm more than good. The fear of death makes a person come to the self-realization of the futility of worldly affairs and materialistic achievements as evident in the doctor\u2019s narrow escape from death.\nTo understand all important concepts and underlying themes and answer questions as per the CBSE standards, download the NCERT Solutions for Class 9 English Beehive Chapter 5 The Snake and the Mirror PDF for free. Refer to them to give your exam preparation the right direction.\nThe NCERT Solutions for Class 9 English Beehive Chapter 5 The Snake and the Mirror have been created by our top English experts to ensure students have access to clear and concise solutions to all NCERT Textbook questions and other exercises provided in the chapter. A detailed study of the chapter followed by a thorough understanding of the topics and answers discussed in the Solutions will enable students to solve every question in the exam and score high marks.\nChapter 5 English Class 9 NCERT Solutions Beehive - Weightage Marks\nSolving the NCERT Class 9 English Beehive Chapter 5 solutions will provide students with a better perspective so as to understand how one should allot their time to different sections in the paper. The NCERT English Class 9 Chapter 5 solutions are an essential part of Class 9 exam. The Class 9 English Beehive ch 5 paper duration is for two hours, and the overall weightage is 15 marks. The solutions cover every line described in the subjects.\nNCERT Solutions for Class 9 English Beehive Chapter 5 Analysis\nSection 1 \u2013 Before Being Consumed by Pride\nChapter 5 English Class 9 Beehive is humorous prose where the main protagonist is a homoeopathic doctor who went from falling in love with his reflection to fearing for his own life. This story begins with the author narrating about his close encounter with death due to his loss of humility.\nOn a summer night the doctor walked into his rented room, unaware of events that were about to unfold that night. He opened his windows and sat down to read a book. While studying his medical journal, he was interrupted by a mirror that sported his reflection.\nSection 2 - The Part When the Doctor is Overcome With Pride\nAs Ch 5 English Class 9 beehive progresses, his own youthful beauty seemed quite attractive to him, causing different misconceptions to form in his mind. Readers will notice a rise in malicious pride and loss of virtue within the doctor in this part of the prose. He went from simply admiring himself to planning his future marriage. He even wished to marry a rich doctor.\nSection 3 - The Moment of Realisation\nWith the doctor's trail of imagination in regards to admiring himself, he failed to notice the silence in his rat-infested home. As a snake slithered its ways to the doctor's shoulders, he began regretting his own actions. It is here in Beehive Class 9, Chapter 5 that the doctor realises that it was an act of punishment from God, for his vainglory. His fear awakened him from his malicious thinking and made him regret his actions immediately. As the doctor begged for forgiveness, the snake slithered from his shoulders towards the mirror, admiring its own reflection.\nUsing that opportunity, the doctor fled the scene to a friend's place for the night. As he came back the next morning, he was surprised to find only a dirty vest is left behind, while other contents are missing.\nMoral of the Story\nWith the story coming to an end, readers realise how sometimes our pride makes us forget how simple we humans can be. It makes us aware of how easily pride can make and break us. Therefore it is essential for every being to keep their feet on the ground, no matter how high they aim.\nNCERT Solutions For Class 9 English Beehive Chapter 5 Exercises\nFill in the Blanks\nIn NCERT solutions for Class 9 English Beehive Chapter 5, the Snake and the Mirror fill in the blanks to help candidates learn about the story in detail. This segment uses various storylines and leaves one section blank for students to fill up.\nMatching Meaning With the Words\nFrom this Class 9 English the Snake and the Mirror chapter students will understand the meaning of italicised words in a sentence. Inclusion of this exercise is to help students increase their vocabulary.\nReport Questions by Using the 5 Ws\nCh 5 Beehive Class 9 consists of interrogative questions that use lines from the story to test how much the student knows about the chapter. A dialogue is placed within quotes, followed by a set of questions based on it.\nUnderstanding the Meaning of a Sentence\nEvery sentence in literature holds some meaning which a student is required to comprehend after reading the chapter well. That is why, with the help of this exercise in NCERT solutions for Class 9 English Beehive Chapter 5, the snake and the mirror, students get a grasp over the chapter.\nBenefits of NCERT Solutions for Class 9 English Beehive Chapter 5\nWith the help of NCERT solution Class 9 English Beehive Chapter 5 in Vedantu, students can avail the following benefits:\nLanguage in these solutions is quite simple.\nQuestion and Answer format is followed to reduce the burden on students.\nDifferent types of exercises are included for better comprehension.\nReferring to CBSE Class 9 English Chapter 5 solutions available on Vedantu will allow students to score well in upcoming examinations.\nConclusion\nExploring\nNCERT Solutions for Class 9 English Chapter 5\n- \"The Snake and the Mirror\" culminates in a deeper understanding of human fears and resilience. This insightful chapter unveils the intricate balance between fear, courage, and self-reflection, offering valuable lessons about confronting adversities. Embracing the journey of the protagonist, this chapter instills profound insights into human emotions and resilience, leaving readers enriched with timeless wisdom.\nImportant Study Material Links for Class 9 Chapter 5\nS.No.\nStudy Material Links for Chapter 5 The Snake And The Mirror\n1\nClass 9 The Snake And The Mirror Revision Notes\n2\nClass 9 The Snake And The Mirror Important Questions\nChapters-wise NCERT Class 9 English Beehive\nS.No.\nNCERT Class 9 English Beehive Chapters"
